##Description

This project demonstrates the use of HTML and CSS selectors to style web page elements without using inline CSS. It includes element selectors, class selectors, ID selectors, pseudo-classes, and list styling.

##Features
Styled headings using class selectors
Styled elements using ID selectors
Paragraph styling with element selectors
Ordered and unordered list styling
Highlighted text using the <mark> tag
Hyperlinks without inline CSS
Clean and simple webpage layout

##Technologies Used 
HTML5
CSS3
Files
index.html – Main HTML file
style.css – CSS stylesheet
README.md – Project documentation


##How to Run
Download or clone the project.
Open index.html in any web browser.
The webpage will display the styled output.

##Learning Outcomes
Understanding CSS selectors
Applying classes and IDs
Styling lists and links
Using pseudo-classes like :hover
Separating HTML structure from CSS styling